# 02 Data Synchronization Strategy

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant LS as 💾 LocalStorage
    participant SE as 🔄 Sync Engine
    participant API as 📡 REST API
    participant DB as 🏠 Database

    Note over User, DB: Phase 1: Authentication & Discovery
    User->>LS: Saves Project & Tasks (Guest)
    User->>API: Login(Google/Email)
    API-->>User: JWT & UserID

    Note over User, DB: Phase 2: Client & Project Sync
    SE->>LS: getLocalClients()
    SE->>API: POST /api/sync/clients (Batch)
    API->>DB: createMany(clients)
    DB-->>API: New Client UUIDs {oldId: newId}
    API-->>SE: Map {clientMap}

    SE->>LS: getLocalProjects()
    SE->>SE: mapClientIds(projects, clientMap)
    SE->>API: POST /api/sync/projects (Batch)
    API->>DB: createMany(projects)
    DB-->>API: New Project UUIDs {oldId: newId}
    API-->>SE: Map {projectMap}

    Note over User, DB: Phase 3: Tasks, Subtasks & Notes
    SE->>LS: getLocalTasks()
    SE->>SE: mapProjectIds(tasks, projectMap)
    SE->>API: POST /api/sync/tasks (Batch)
    API->>DB: createMany(tasks_with_subtasks)
    DB-->>API: New Task UUIDs
    
    SE->>LS: getLocalNotes()
    SE->>SE: mapGroupIds(notes, clientMap, projectMap)
    SE->>API: POST /api/sync/notes (Batch)
    API->>DB: createMany(notes)
    
    Note over User, DB: Phase 4: Finalization
    SE->>LS: Clear Synced Data
    API-->>User: Success (Reload Dashboard)
```

### Story: Maintaining Referential Integrity
The most critical part of the sync is not just moving data, but **preserving relationships**. By mapping old local IDs (cuid-like) to new PostgreSQL UUIDs in memory during the process, we ensure that a Task created locally as "Task A" belonging to "Project X" is correctly re-assigned to the *newly created* "Project X" on the server.
